AEDoor.library: keep the caller's d1/a0/a1 across every call, as AEDoor 2.x does.

NilBBS's register stubs clobber d1/a0/a1.  The Quest (hand-written assembler)
keeps its DIFace in a1 across calls and then wrote through garbage, clobbering
low memory including SysBase at $4.  movem around each stub fixes it and leaves
the condition codes the docs promise alone.  Offered upstream to NilBBS.
Against NilBBS 4f9c0c3, apply with: patch -p1 < this file (from the NilBBS root).

--- a/src/aedoor/aedoor_start.S
+++ b/src/aedoor/aedoor_start.S
@@ -169,19 +169,24 @@
 |   ...  (flags: 1 = string given, 2 = data given)
 
 LCreateComm:                    | d0 = node (ASCII, obsolete)
+    movem.l d1/a0-a1,-(sp)      | ENiGMA: keep the caller's d1/a0/a1, as AEDoor 2.x does
     move.l  d0,-(sp)
     jsr     _aed_CreateComm
     addq.l  #4,sp
     tst.l   d0
+    movem.l (sp)+,d1/a0-a1      | (movem leaves the condition codes alone)
     rts
 
 LDeleteComm:                    | a1 = dif
